+# WA Vault v0.5.6 — batch-delete cap hotfix
+
+- Fixes the case where six (or more) consecutive text messages are deleted together but Android/WhatsApp exposes only four deletion-marker rows.
+- The deletion target can now expand beyond the marker count from two independent sources: the active per-conversation burst ledger and a DB-backed compact recent-message cluster.
+- The DB fallback only walks the newest undeleted messages, requires consecutive gaps <= 20 s, and caps the whole cluster to <= 90 s to avoid sweeping older chat history into the batch.
+- Example: 6 consecutive captured messages + replacement exposing 4 deletion markers -> aggressive target becomes 6 and the existing DB fallback can mark the remaining two rows.
+- Keeps v0.5.5 dedupe, aggressive media/audio capture, and fast multi-selection unchanged.
+- Adds diagnostics: last_delete_marker_count, last_delete_ledger_count, last_delete_db_burst_count, last_delete_target, DELETE_MARKER_CAP_EXPANDED.
+
+This still depends on Android/WhatsApp notification data. It cannot recover message content that WA Vault never captured before deletion.
